1
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and
even my shoe went flying.

3
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:32,920
onto the head of the carpenter
I was putting in a chokehold,

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,120
and they laughed that
I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
one yawn later, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,220
From the pointed hat's water bottle,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset falls into the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too, it'll all end just like this

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:20,980
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness too is lost again.

12
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:24,560
I only realized it too late,
because I'm such an idiot.

13
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:40,620
Enomoto-san,
any further discussion is pointless.

14
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:43,420
I'll go alone.

15
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,400
Hijikata-kun.

16
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,920
We are the flowers that bloomed
at the end of the Bakumatsu,

17
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:57,760
and we must scatter when the new era comes.

18
00:01:59,260 --> 00:01:59,920
Sorry.

19
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:02,380
Hijikata-kun, wait!

20
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:04,480
What good will it do for you to die alone?

21
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,620
Next time: Flower of the Bakumatsu

22
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:15,700
Please look forward to the final episode.

23
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:17,980
Makes you cry no matter
how many times you watch it.

24
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:22,860
Even if you go against
the tide of the times,

25
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:25,000
living without bending your own convictions.

26
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,320
Being swept along by every silly fad,

27
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:29,420
playing around all night long.

28
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:30,640
The young people these days

29
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,700
should learn a thing or two from this.

30
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:40,040
This, no, it was this one, right?

31
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:42,820
I knew it, it's this one.

32
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:45,300
Ah, no good.

33
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:48,320
Um, street

34
00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:25,000


35
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:55,440
Damn it!

36
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:57,080
Fine!

37
00:03:57,580 --> 00:03:58,480
Hey, pull yourself together!

38
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:05,140
You two have forgotten how to use things,
haven't you?

39
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,460
Your eyes are hopeless, after all.

40
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:09,880
Never mind that, just fix it quickly!

41
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:12,640
Why don't you just pull the plug?

42
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:13,140
Yes.

43
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:15,580
Hey, Duck. Wait a moment.

44
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:18,100
Sensei, will I become a pilot?

45
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:19,580
Why?

46
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:20,280
Do your best!

47
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:29,200
Uh uh uh

48
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:42,420
Wow, did that show really
go over a 30% ratings share?

49
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:44,400
That's the one about the Bakumatsu, right?

50
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:46,240
Komachi and the others said
they're watching it too.

51
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:50,540
My wife's totally hooked on it too. She's
watching it instead of doing the housework.

52
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:54,580
The Chief apparently records every episode on
video and watches each one at least three times.

53
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,720
That's right, the Chief is a huge
fan of this kind of period drama.

54
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:02,900
You lot, what on earth have you
been talking about this whole time?

55
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:05,400
We're talking about the
period drama on TV, sir.

56
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:08,380
You've never seen Flower of the Bakumatsu,
Ryo-san?

57
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:09,900
Flower of the Bakumatsu?

58
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:10,940
Seriously?

59
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:13,560
Ryo-chan, you really don't know it?

60
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:16,820
That's unusual, coming from a senior
who's so obsessed with ratings.

61
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:20,720
Nope, nope. The only TV I watch
is documentaries and variety shows.

62
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:24,000
Otherwise I watch videos
or act as a game monitor.

63
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,680
Hah! Achoo!

64
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,960
G-good morning!

65
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:34,440
That's why your head is still
at elementary school level!

66
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,220
Ahaha, Chief!

67
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:42,380
At your age, building model trains on the job again!
You idiot!

68
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:44,020
No, I wasn't doing anything!

69
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:51,180
Don't try to hide it, I know! Watching a video, you say?
It's bound to be that filthy stuff! You never improve!

70
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,940
What's the harm?
Let people watch whatever they like.

71
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:58,220
Chief, tonight is finally the final episode of 幕末の花,
isn't it?

72
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:00,820
Yes, that's right.

73
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:04,340
Speaking of which, I'm sorry,
but I have a favor to ask.

74
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:05,920
Me?

75
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:09,260
Tonight's night shift is Terai and Ryotsu,
as it happens.

76
00:06:09,260 --> 00:06:11,080
Ryotsu is unreliable, so

77
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:13,860
Well, I don't want to be relied on either.

78
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:14,780
What did you say?

79
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:16,400
Now, now, Chief.

80
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:19,540
By the way, Terai,
what's this favor you want?

81
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:22,620
I'm sorry to ask this while you're on duty,

82
00:06:22,670 --> 00:06:26,600
could you record the final episode
of 幕末の花 on the police box's video?

83
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:30,880
You see, our VCR broke,
and we've sent it out for repairs.

84
00:06:31,780 --> 00:06:33,700
In that case, it's no trouble at all.

85
00:06:33,980 --> 00:06:37,260
Thank you, I'd appreciate it. I'm away on a business trip tonight,
so I can't watch it.

86
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,420
Yes, leave it to me, Chief.

87
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:49,200
I'm tired.

88
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:52,220
Think I'll take a little break.

89
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,500
The one I was aiming for.

90
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:56,680
Let's see...

91
00:06:58,180 --> 00:07:00,720
December 7th, starting at 10 p.m.

92
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:03,300
Ends at 10:56, got it.

93
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:04,760
Yeah, no mistake about it.

94
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:07,320
But I'm worried whether
it'll actually record properly.

95
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:08,660
I'll just watch it right here.

96
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:13,120
A low-pressure system that has developed to
typhoon strength is approaching the Kanto region.

97
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:15,240
What are you doing over there?

98
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:18,880
I'm recording 幕末の花,
the one the Chief asked me to tape.

99
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:21,720
If you're recording,
just set the timer and be done with it.

100
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:23,520
No, don't touch it!

101
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:25,780
I did set the timer,

102
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:28,580
but if it doesn't work,
there's no fixing it.

103
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:31,520
I'm responsible,
since the Chief asked me to do it.

104
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:33,160
I have to double-check it properly.

105
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:35,520
You really are a worrywart.

106
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:40,040
Fine, then stay there and glare at the screen
to your heart's content while it records.

107
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,460
I will.

108
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:42,720
Just leave me alone.

109
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:44,260
It starts in ten minutes, after all.

110
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:47,260
What's the point of having a timer,
honestly?

111
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:54,680
Did something get unplugged?

112
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:59,480
I can't tell which outlet is which.

113
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:02,800
Okay.

114
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:06,560
Oh no, did I do it?

115
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,140
Ryo-san, we've got a problem!

116
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:12,980
It's a blackout!

117
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:14,580
We must have used too much electricity.

118
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:18,000
But it starts in five minutes!

119
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:21,840
Is that so? Don't worry about it.

120
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:24,300
I can fix it in a minute.

121
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:30,900
It's no good.
The switchboard has completely burned out.

122
00:08:31,460 --> 00:08:32,520
It can't be repaired.

123
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:34,360
Why did it come to this?

124
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:37,240
Now that you mention it,
the last time a fuse blew,

125
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:39,440
maybe using wire as a
substitute was a mistake.

126
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:42,680
W-what are we going to do, Ryo-san?
The show's about to start!

127
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:45,240
If it's come to this,
we'd better accept defeat gracefully.

128
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:49,320
No way. The Chief asked us to do this.

129
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:51,040
I didn't get asked.

130
00:08:51,540 --> 00:08:52,780
How heartless.

131
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:56,420
I'll just tell him it's because
of Ryo-san's model trains.

132
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:58,140
That's bad.

133
00:08:58,140 --> 00:08:59,680
Bad or not, I'll tell him.

134
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:02,300
If it comes to this,
I'm going down with you, Ryo-san.

135
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:03,540
Wait, wait, okay, I get it.

136
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:07,740
If there's no electricity here, we just
need to go where there is electricity.

137
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:09,460
Where to?

138
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:18,000
We're running out of time!

139
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,440
Right, let's take it from there.

140
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:29,000
What are you going to do
with a vending machine?

141
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:31,980
I'm just going to unplug this one's power.

142
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:34,060
Are you all right, Ryo-san?

143
00:09:34,060 --> 00:09:35,280
There, that's done.

144
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:36,860
How many minutes left?

145
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:39,020
We only have three minutes left, Ryo-san!

146
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:41,700
Okay, three minutes is plenty, plenty!

147
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:47,960
Ryo-san, it's still not showing!

148
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:50,080
That's strange.

149
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:52,500
Right, I forgot the antenna!

150
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,760
W-what do we do?

151
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:56,980
We didn't even bring an antenna!

152
00:09:56,980 --> 00:09:58,760
There's only two minutes left!

153
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:01,340
Right, find something
to use as a substitute!

154
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:03,040
N-no, s-substitute... like what?

155
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:06,180
Right, that's it!

156
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:09,400
No way, Ryo-san,
there's only one minute left!

157
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:10,320
Don't give up!

158
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:13,060
Plug in the cable!

159
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:30,180
Ryo-san, what are you doing? Hurry up!

160
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:32,800
Damn it, saying whatever you want!

161
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:42,540
How about now?

162
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:48,980
No good, Ryo-san.
Nothing's showing up at all!

163
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,320
Nope, nope.

164
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,040
This one...

165
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,460
A little more.

166
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:57,560
How about this time?

167
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,360
Amazing, Ryo-san!

168
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,220
It's showing!

169
00:11:02,220 --> 00:11:03,320
See? What did I tell you?

170
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:06,160
Nothing is impossible for me.

171
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:18,860
Are you okay, Ryo-san?

172
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:21,980
I nearly died.

173
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:24,860
Ryo-san.

174
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:27,900
Thanks for your hard work.

175
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:31,860
How did it go, Ryo-san?

176
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:36,760
Looks like the antenna
was just too much for it.

177
00:11:38,020 --> 00:11:41,040
What am I supposed to tell the Chief?
That's awful, Ryo-san.

178
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,940
We did everything we could to fix it,
so it can't be helped.

179
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:46,440
If you hadn't caused the blackout,
we could have recorded it properly.

180
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:48,600
That was an accident. It couldn't be helped.

181
00:11:48,860 --> 00:11:50,580
An accident doesn't cut it!

182
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:53,060
It's the show the Chief
was looking forward to!

183
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:54,720
Hey, calm down, will you!

184
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:55,380
Ouch!

185
00:11:59,060 --> 00:12:02,200
Just say we recorded it
properly onto this video!

186
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:04,020
He'll know right away once he watches it!

187
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:06,980
Nobody will know unless
they play it back, right?

188
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:11,620
In other words, we just need something
to happen before the Chief watches it.

189
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:13,000
Heh heh.

190
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,500
Chief, welcome back.

191
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:32,240
Good work.

192
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:36,120
What do we do? The chief's finally back!

193
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:40,100
Don't panic. Listen, leave this to me.

194
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:43,720
Chief, thank you for your hard work.

195
00:12:44,220 --> 00:12:46,720
In this cold,
it must have been really tough.

196
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:50,000
Yeah, well, where's Terai?

197
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:53,240
Terai? You mean last night's video.

198
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:55,760
The video's right here, all set.

199
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:56,940
Last night's?

200
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,260
Did you manage to record it properly?

201
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:02,260
Come on, Chief! Of course I have it!

202
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:06,380
Even if an earthquake hits or a storm comes,
I'd never forget!

203
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:07,200
Hey, Terai!

204
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:08,780
Hey, Terai!

205
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:10,380
Terai!

206
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:11,440
Y-yes!

207
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:14,840
I see, I see.
Sorry about that. No, thank you.

208
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:17,620
Well, I'll hand it over to the Chief.
Here you go.

209
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,400
No, please hold off, Chief!

210
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:23,060
W-what?

211
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:25,000
Please stop, Chief!

212
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:29,120
Chief! What on earth are you doing?

213
00:13:30,860 --> 00:13:31,620
You do it, then.

214
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:41,560
The tape of Bakumatsu no Hana -

215
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:43,840
What on earth are you doing?

216
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:45,920
After I went to the trouble
of recording the video for you,

217
00:13:46,820 --> 00:13:47,660
Fine, I get it.

218
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:50,760
The chief hates me,
so he played a cruel trick on me!

219
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:52,840
That must be it.

220
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:56,180
No, that's not it at all.

221
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:57,760
It just happened in the heat of the moment.

222
00:13:57,760 --> 00:13:58,880
You demon of a chief!

223
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:01,972
Ryo-chan,

224
00:14:02,022 --> 00:14:04,960
Did you really record the final
episode of Bakumatsu no Hana?

225
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:06,160
Of course!

226
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:10,180
That wonderful final scene,

227
00:14:10,230 --> 00:14:13,060
even now, just remembering it,
my chest aches with emotion.

228
00:14:16,780 --> 00:14:20,420
Don't stop me, Mom. Meiji is calling me.

229
00:14:20,740 --> 00:14:22,690
I must go.

230
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:25,240
I must go!

231
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:30,660
That final line was just wonderful.

232
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:32,920
Ryo-chan, Ryo-chan.

233
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:37,580
Last night's Bakumatsu no Hana was
cancelled because of a news special.

234
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:44,020
The final episode will now air next week.

235
00:14:44,020 --> 00:14:45,400
N-n-n-n-n-n-n...

236
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:47,580
Ryo-chaaan.

237
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:51,600
Ah, wait... was it?

238
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:57,340
You idiot! I won't tolerate your attitude of
making excuses and trying to cover up your mistakes!

239
00:14:57,660 --> 00:15:01,400
Your whole life is one big cover-up!
Reflect on yourself!

240
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:09,700
My EF58!

241
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:10,940
How should I know about that!

242
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:15,340
Chief, I'm truly sorry.

243
00:15:15,340 --> 00:15:16,581
Forget it.

244
00:15:16,631 --> 00:15:19,700
It's all Ryotsu's fault. The aim wasn't bad.

245
00:15:19,700 --> 00:15:20,740
Damn it!

246
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:23,900
I won't let this grudge go unanswered.

247
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:27,760
Just you wait.

248
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:30,920
You have no idea how terrifying it
is to turn me into a vengeful demon,

249
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:34,260
I risked my life for the chief,

250
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:36,360
climbing a utility pole in the wind!

251
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:39,080
It's all because the chief
is a machine-hating blockhead,

252
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:40,260
which is why this happened.

253
00:15:40,260 --> 00:15:43,280
He's bound to have no
idea how to use a VCR deck.

254
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:45,240
Well, for my part,

255
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:47,720
